+# Educational text cards (7.0.74)
+
+Applies only when a video's content type is **education** (the default type,
+also used by cooking, health, self-care, business and farming presets). Other
+video types keep the 7.0.73 cards exactly as before.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Five-point box.** Gemini Web can return a `points` card: a title and 3–5 short
+  points (each at most 60 characters), anchored to the spoken list. It lasts 6–14
+  seconds. The box is a translucent panel with numbered rows.
+- **Single-point cards.** Three new kinds, each with a glyph badge:
+  - `takeaway` (star, "KEY IDEA")
+  - `tip` (check, "TRY THIS")
+  - `warning` (triangle, "AVOID THIS")
+  Each is one line of at most 80 characters and lasts 2–6 seconds.
+- **Open and close animation.** Educational cards and list panels pop open (scale
+  70% → 100%, eased, with a fade-in) and close (shrink to 80% with a fade-out). The
+  animation is applied in the FFmpeg overlay graph, so it works in normal and
+  bounded renders. Other video types are not animated.
+- **Playful look.** For educational videos with card style set to *auto*, cards use
+  the playful palette. An explicit card style is respected.
+- **Structured list graphics.** `production/graphics.json` list events also pop in
+  educational videos.
+
+## Content rules (Gemini Web)
+
+- Only facts stated in the narration. No invented facts, statistics or numbers.
+- Kinds: `takeaway`, `tip`, `warning`, `points`. Any other kind is rejected.
+- Non-educational videos ignore `kind` and `points`. Their drafts stay plain keypoint cards.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+- The speech-card fingerprint includes a variant tag for educational drafts.
+  Non-educational fingerprints are unchanged, so existing drafts stay valid.
+  An educational render refuses a non-educational draft, and the reverse, until the
+  drafting step is run again.
+- Language editions still use their own card path from 7.0.73. Educational
+  cards are not applied to edition copies in this release.
+- Speech cards remain opt-in (the Create option "Use speech-timed Gemini cards").
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tests/test_v774_educational_cards.py`: validation, both orientations, transparent
+  panel, the pop animation rendered through FFmpeg (area measured at 0.5, 1.12, 2.5,
+  3.9 and 4.6 seconds), prompt selection, fingerprints, and structured list gating.
+- Targeted suites that touch cards and audio pass, except the 10 typography and
+  finishing failures already present on 7.0.73 and the ffprobe-dependent test in the
+  sandbox.
+
+## Install
+
+From 7.0.73: `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.74/tools/update_v773_to_v774.py .` (dry
+run), then the same with `--apply`. Stop the dashboard first. Installs on 7.0.70 run
+`update_v770_to_v771.py`, `update_v771_to_v772.py`, `update_v772_to_v773.py`, then
+this one.
